  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0:\n  What's changed\n  - Added TALXIS Portal support: set \"target\": \"Portal\" in appsettings.json and the login, navigation, form, subgrid, command and dialog steps run against the portal.\n  - Added steps for file downloads, record access and portal row commands, and {{TODAY}} / {{TODAY:+n}} dates in step values.\n  - Fixed the package missing the MSBuild task for @extends data files, which failed every build with MSB4062 in 1.0.10. The task now also works on Linux and macOS.\n  - Moved the packages to .NET 10.\n  - Updated Selenium to 4.52.0 and removed the DotNetSeleniumExtras.WaitHelpers dependency.\n  - The business process flow stage step is now reported as pending instead of passing without checking the stage.\n\n  Impact\n  - Minor release: projects must target net10.0. Older projects stop with TESTKIT001.\n  - Projects that reference Selenium directly need 4.52.0 or later.\n\n1.0.10:\n  NuGet icon\n  - Added the new TestKit package icon to published packages\n  - Embedded package readme and repository metadata consistently across packages\n\n  Release workflow alignment\n  - Switched publishing from push-to-master to GitHub Release / workflow_dispatch\n  - Added release-tag-based version resolution (vX.Y.Z)\n  - Matched the pack → artifact upload → deploy flow used in the other TALXIS package repos\n\n  Deployment fix\n  - Switched NuGet publishing to OIDC-based login, matching the working TALXIS release pattern used in tools-devkit-build\n  - Kept the explicit build-then-pack flow that succeeds on GitHub's Windows runner\n\n1.0.9:\n  NuGet icon\n  - Added the new TestKit package icon to published packages\n  - Embedded package readme and repository metadata consistently across packages\n\n  Release workflow alignment\n  - Switched publishing from push-to-master to GitHub Release / workflow_dispatch\n  - Added release-tag-based version resolution (vX.Y.Z)\n  - Matched the pack → artifact upload → deploy flow used in the other TALXIS package repos\n\n  Packaging fixes\n  - Moved to unified 1.0.9 package versioning across TestKit packages\n  - Updated Bindings to pack cleanly with the Selectors projects from the same solution\n  - Fixed the Windows release workflow to build first, then pack with --no-build\n\n1.0.8:\n  NuGet icon\n  - Added the new TestKit package icon to published packages\n  - Embedded package readme and repository metadata consistently across packages\n\n  Release workflow alignment\n  - Switched publishing from push-to-master to GitHub Release / workflow_dispatch\n  - Added release-tag-based version resolution (vX.Y.Z)\n  - Matched the pack → artifact upload → deploy flow used in the other TALXIS package repos\n\n  Packaging fixes\n  - Moved to unified 1.0.8 package versioning across TestKit packages\n  - Updated Bindings to pack cleanly with the Selectors projects from the same solution\n  - Fixed the publish workflow to pack each publishable project explicitly on Windows\n\n1.0.7:\n  NuGet icon\n  - Added the new TestKit package icon to published packages\n  - Embedded package readme and repository metadata consistently across packages\n\n  Release workflow alignment\n  - Switched publishing from push-to-master to GitHub Release / workflow_dispatch\n  - Added release-tag-based version resolution (vX.Y.Z)\n  - Matched the pack → artifact upload → deploy flow used in the other TALXIS package repos\n\n  Packaging fixes\n  - Set the shared package version baseline to 1.0.7\n  - Updated Bindings to pack cleanly with the Selectors projects from the same solution\n  - Removed the stale package icon wiring from the Bindings project in favor of shared package metadata",
